---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Link from "../../components/Link.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Autowealth + CompoundFox — Algo trading platform with live performance dashboard | Alejandro Martínez"
  description="Built CompoundFox algorithmic trading strategy and Autowealth, its SaaS distribution platform. Live performance dashboard at stats.autowealth.trade: deposit-adjusted drawdown, Sharpe, TWR and Sortino calculated from real Bybit trade history. Per-community ECS via CDK, on-chain fee settlement, AUM circuit breaker. Sole engineer."
>
  <div class="page">

    <!-- top bar -->
    <header class="topbar">
      <Brand />
      <nav class="topbar-nav">
        <Link href="/">← back</Link>
        <Link href="/#case-studies">case studies</Link>
        <Link href="mailto:alex@konar.es">contact</Link>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- hero -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-tag">CASE STUDY · 06</div>
        <div class="hero-main">
          <div class="hero-meta">ALGORITHMIC TRADING · DISTRIBUTION PLATFORM &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2025 — NOW &nbsp;·&nbsp; SOLE ENGINEER</div>
          <h1 class="hero-h1">CompoundFox: live algo trading with a public, defensible performance record.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Autowealth is a SaaS platform that distributes algorithmic trading strategies to followers
            across Bybit, Binance, and Hyperliquid. CompoundFox is the flagship strategy, live since
            November 2025 with a logic revision shipped in February 2026 and a risk-per-trade
            increase currently rolling out. Live performance is published at stats.autowealth.trade:
            equity curve, Sharpe, deposit-adjusted drawdown, and TWR calculated in real time from
            actual Bybit trade history. No backtest, no screenshot. Per-community ECS containers,
            an on-chain fee Splitter, and an AUM circuit breaker make the platform multi-tenant and
            production-grade.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <div class="hero-links-label">LINKS</div>
          <Link href="https://autowealth.trade" class="hero-link">autowealth.trade ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://stats.autowealth.trade" class="hero-link">stats.autowealth.trade ↗</Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- numbers strip -->
    <div class="numbers">
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">STATUS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">live · public dashboard</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">stats.autowealth.trade · refreshed daily</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">AUM SNAPSHOTS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">every 5 min</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">288 snapshots/day · circuit breaker after 3 failures</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">EXCHANGES</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">3 supported</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">bybit (master) · binance · hyperliquid (followers)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">ON-CHAIN BILLING</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">Solidity Splitter</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">bsc + arbitrum · hd wallet derivation</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell numbers-cell--last">
        <div class="numbers-key">DEPLOYMENT</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">per-community ECS</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">cdk · one container per community id</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the brief -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="THE BRIEF" title="A trading strategy with proof.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Most algo strategies are sold on backtests or cherry-picked screenshots. Autowealth publishes
        live performance: full equity curve, Sharpe, drawdown, and TWR pulled from real Bybit trade
        history and updated daily on a public dashboard. Anyone can check it before committing capital.
        CompoundFox is the flagship strategy. Autowealth is the platform behind it: copy trading across
        three exchanges, per-community deployment, and on-chain fee invoicing.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- architecture -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="ARCHITECTURE" title="Turborepo monorepo: backend, bot, dashboards, mobile, infra.">
      <pre class="arch-diagram">  ┌─ Turborepo monorepo
  │
  ├── apps/
  │   ├── backend              [ Bun · TypeScript · Drizzle · PostgreSQL ]
  │   │      Bybit API integration · AUM snapshotting · performance calculation
  │   │      on-chain fee invoicing · position deduplication
  │   │
  │   ├── telegram-bot         [ Telegraf · TypeScript ]
  │   │      strategy signals · performance alerts · follower management
  │   │
  │   ├── performance-page     [ Next.js · React Query ]
  │   │      live equity curve · Sharpe · deposit-adjusted drawdown · TWR
  │   │      startBalanceReliable flag: hides metrics it can't defend
  │   │
  │   └── mobile               [ React Native ]
  │          strategy overview · performance charts · notifications
  │
  ├── packages/
  │   ├── database             [ Drizzle · PostgreSQL · 7 migrations ]
  │   └── sweep-service        [ Solidity Splitter · Hardhat · BSC + Arbitrum ]
  │
  └── cdk/                     [ TypeScript · AWS CDK ]
         ExchangeBotStack per community · shared VPC/cluster via CF exports
         512MB / 0.25 CPU per bot · VPS Docker alternative
</pre>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- decisions -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="DECISIONS" title="Six calls that define the platform.">
      <div class="decisions-grid">
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">01 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Deposit-adjusted drawdown with 3-day attribution</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Raw AUM drawdown inflates whenever a deposit lands: AUM spikes, then the strategy looks like it immediately lost capital. The performance engine walks a 3-day attribution window to match transaction amounts to AUM jumps before computing peak-to-trough. The window exists because of a production failure: late-day deposits landing after the daily snapshot produced phantom -100% drawdowns until the attribution logic was added.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">02 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Reliability tiers: hide numbers that can't be defended</div>
          <p class="decision-body">The performance API returns a <code>startBalanceReliable</code> flag when there is no AUM snapshot before the first trade. When the flag is false, the UI hides annualized return and average monthly return entirely. The dashboard doesn't fill in a guess; it shows fewer numbers. Accounts that connected mid-strategy get a smaller metrics set until a full pre-trade snapshot exists.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">03 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">AUM circuit breaker isolates dead API keys</div>
          <p class="decision-body">A snapshot job that retries every failing account wastes cycles on expired keys and slows down active ones. The worker in <code>snapshotAUM.ts</code> tracks consecutive failures per account in a <code>Map&lt;string, number&gt;</code>, skips accounts with 3+ consecutive failures, and resets the count hourly. An <code>isRunning</code> guard prevents concurrent execution without a lock library. One expired API key has no effect on the snapshot cadence of live accounts. The job runs every 5 minutes (288 snapshots/day per active account).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">04 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Position deduplication via 8-decimal-place PnL fingerprint</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Not all exchange APIs return stable order IDs across paginated history endpoints. Bybit's position history in particular doesn't guarantee idempotent IDs. The worker in <code>processNewClosedPositions.ts</code> uses a 5-field composite key: exchange + account UID + symbol + side + timestamp + PnL formatted to 8 decimal places via <code>formatToPrecision8()</code>, matching the <code>decimal(18,8)</code> DB column. The fingerprint check in <code>positionExists()</code> runs before every write. Positions are fetched in 7-day chunks with 100ms rate-limit delays to stay within Bybit's pagination limits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">05 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Per-community ECS containers via CDK</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Each trading community gets its own exchange-bot container, not a shared bot with multi-tenant config. The CDK stack (<code>ExchangeBotStack</code>) takes a <code>communityId</code> as a prop and deploys into a shared ECS cluster imported via CloudFormation cross-stack exports (<code>InfrastructureClusterArn</code>, <code>InfrastructureVPCId</code>). Adding a community is a <code>deploy-exchange-bot.sh COMMUNITY_ID TOKEN</code> call. For operators who want lower AWS costs, a Docker VPS alternative runs the same container at 512MB / 0.25 CPU with the same isolation guarantee per community ID.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">06 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">On-chain fee settlement via Solidity Splitter</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Trading fees invoiced to followers go into a Hardhat-tested Solidity Splitter contract on BSC and Arbitrum that distributes to provider, platform, and referral wallets atomically. Each trader's wallet is derived deterministically via <code>BSCWalletService.deriveTraderWallet(traderId, communityId)</code>, so wallets don't need manual provisioning per follower. The pipeline runs fully automated: position close triggers invoice, invoice triggers on-chain sweep. Coverage data shows 40+ contract statements exercised in tests.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ownership -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OWNERSHIP" title="The full stack, built and shipped sole.">
      <div class="ownership-scroll"><div class="ownership">
        <div class="ownership-header">
          <span>COMPONENT</span>
          <span>STACK</span>
          <span class="text-right">ROLE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Trading backend</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">bun · typescript · drizzle · postgresql · bybit api</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Performance engine</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">1,334-line trade-analysis.ts · sharpe · twr · sortino · calmar</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Performance page</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">next.js · react query · live equity curve · reliability tiers</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Telegram bot</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">telegraf · typescript · strategy signals · follower management</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">React Native mobile</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">react native · performance charts · notifications</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Sweep service</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">solidity splitter · hardhat · bsc + arbitrum · hd wallet derivation</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">AWS infrastructure</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">typescript · aws cdk · ecs · cloudwatch · rds</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
      </div></div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- outcome -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OUTCOME" title="Live algo trading with public, auditable performance.">
      <p class="body-para">
        CompoundFox is running live on Bybit with performance published at stats.autowealth.trade —
        equity curve, Sharpe, deposit-adjusted drawdown, and TWR calculated from real position
        history by a 1,334-line metrics engine built from scratch. The numbers on the dashboard are
        either defensible or the platform says so: the <code>startBalanceReliable</code> flag hides
        annualized return on accounts without a pre-trade AUM snapshot. Autowealth as a platform
        handles multi-tenant copy trading across three exchanges, per-community ECS deployment
        via CDK, automated on-chain fee settlement, and a circuit breaker that keeps AUM
        snapshotting unblocked when individual API keys expire.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- next case -->
    <div class="next-case">
      <span class="next-case-label">NEXT CASE STUDY</span>
      <Link href="/cases/copy-trader" class="next-case-link">
        07 &nbsp; Copy Trader — Multi-exchange copy trading engine →
      </Link>
    </div>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="footer">
      <span>alejandro martinez · @lyricalstring · oss under konar technologies</span>
      <span>alex@konar.es</span>
    </footer>

  </div>

</Base>


<style>
  @import "../../styles/case-study.css";

  /* ── OWNERSHIP TABLE: autowealth has 3 columns (2fr 3fr 1fr) ── */
  .ownership-header,
  .ownership-row {
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr 1fr;
  }

  /* ── NUMBERS STRIP: autowealth has 5 cells (overrides shared 6-col) ── */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .numbers {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .numbers-cell--last {
    border-right: none;
  }

  /* inline code in decision-body */
  .decision-body code {
    background: #101216;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
</style>
